#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""<the same measurement question as in PROTOCOL-<name>.md, one sentence>

Usage:
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py --show 3
        The config and three feature rows per split; no fit.
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py --probe
        Instrument check: twelve labelled items, reduced estimator at fit
        or the unchanged predictor at apply (its null on permuted labels),
        both lanes, into a throwaway file; prints the scores (not reported)
        and one row per lane as the run will keep them.
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py --calibrate-null
        Apply only, before the registration: the unchanged predictor's
        predictions on the labelled items, fixed, scored against 200
        permutations of their gold; prints their spread and the null_band
        the rule below derives from it. No run, nothing written, and the
        predictions are never scored against their true gold.
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py
        The full run, recorded by runlog (at high repeat cost: `runlog start
        <area> -- …`, after the freeze and the preflight audit).
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py --eval-only
        Re-evaluate the kept rows; no fit.
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py --repeat-of RUN_ID
        The kept run RUN_ID drawn again with a seed labkit derives from it
        and the draw number (`answering_run.repeat_seed`), everything else
        unchanged: a run of its own (repeat_of) into <out>_draw<N>.jsonl —
        the spread over seeds, never the answer. `02_analyze.py --draws`
        shows it.
    ../../.venv/bin/python scripts/01_measure.py --seed 7
        A measurement with another seed: a full run like the one above,
        which answers the protocol when it is the newest — the spread is
        `--repeat-of`, not this.

The protocol's kind chooses the instrument. At `fit`, `make_estimator()`
creates an estimator with fit(X, y) and predict(X): the registered lane
fits true labels, the null lane fits labels permuted inside each fitting
fold, and the test lane fits every labelled item before predicting the
unlabelled split. Every scored prediction is out of fold.
At `apply`, `make_estimator()` loads the unchanged predictor with
predict(X); it is never fitted and never sees gold. Its null lane scores
the same predictions against the gold labels permuted with the seed —
each null row names whose label it carries (`gold_of`) —, so the noise
floor needs no second instrument. What those predictions reach against
randomly assigned labels on average is exact, no draw
(`permutation_expectation()`): [C1]'s bar is it plus `margin`, and [A2]
holds the one permuted draw — the anchor in the same run — within
`null_band` of it. The band comes from the spread the permutation brings
(not a refit, not new model answers), by the rule [A2] registers beside it
(`null_band_quantile` over `null_permutations`, seeded from the run's
seed; `band_by_rule`): `--calibrate-null --write` registers it before the
first measurement, and the first measurement refuses a band the rule does
not give, before its run opens. Without a registered rule the band is a
reasoned value, and `--calibrate-null` shows the fixed rule here
(`NULL_PERMUTATIONS`, `NULL_BAND_QUANTILE`). A protocol that registers a fixed null predictor
returns it from `make_null_predictor()` instead; its score plus `margin`
is the bar, and [A2] holds it within `null_band` of `chance_of()`. At fit
the null lane refits on permuted labels `NULL_REFITS` times, each draw
seeded from the run's seed, its fold and its number: [C1]'s bar is the
mean of their scores plus `margin`, [A2] holds that mean within
`null_band` of `chance_of()`, and the draws' scores (`a2_draw_scores`)
show how far one strays — one refit's draw decided a fit's verdict
(fourth SAB-like draw: `c1_score` = `c1_threshold`). A band changed after the first measurement is
refused (report-check). All lanes are
recorded in the same run (LAB-034 Null condition in the same run).
Unlabelled predictions are never scored.

Measurement contract:
  - Every labelled item is predicted once per scored lane in the same run;
    `fit` uses out-of-fold fitting, `apply` uses unchanged predictors.
  - The score (`SCORE`: accuracy · r2 · auc) is over EVERY labelled item of
    the lane: an item without a prediction scores as wrong (accuracy, auc)
    or as the mean (r2) and is counted on its own as `a1_empty`.
  - [C1] passes when the registered lane's score is at least the bar plus
    `margin`: at apply with the permuted null its exact expectation
    (`permutation_expectation`), at fit the mean of the `NULL_REFITS`
    permuted-label refits, with a fixed null predictor its score.
  - [A1] checks the yield (at most `max_empty` labelled items without a
    prediction); [A2] that the null lane scores within `null_band` of its
    target — the permutation expectation at apply, chance otherwise
    (`chance_of`, derived, not guessed). If either fails, [C1] has no
    verdict (None).
  - A withheld label is no label: the prepare step writes `gold: null` for
    the unlabelled split (a test file storing 0 or -999 is a placeholder),
    and a lane carrying an item without gold is never scored — a criterion
    on zero gold once "passed" (haiku t3, labkit-paper area 09, 2026-10-16).
  - `evaluate_rows()` is the only implementation of these formulas;
    `02_analyze.py` and the test import it, never copy it.
  - The protocol owns the registered thresholds; `MeasureConfig` holds them
    for one execution; config.json records that object whole.
  - A seed is a source of randomness, so the protocol's randomness and
    noise-ceiling fields are owed. Measure the spread on the probe or on
    the null lane; the registered lane on all items before the freeze makes
    the freeze empty (Sonnet v3 t3 and t5, 2026-10-16).

A task that names its output file (`pred_results/<name>.csv`) is answered
by that file: DELIVERABLES names it, deliverable_rows() gives its rows from
the kept rows and the metrics, and the full run writes and registers it
(`write_deliverables`; a repeat's draw writes none) — its sha256 lands in
the run's outputs.json, and `finalize` holds the file in the tree to it.
Never write it by hand.

Why (house rules, one per line so a reference is never cut):
  LAB-034 Null condition in the same run
  LAB-035 Thresholds belong to the run
  LAB-041 Generate numbers, don't retype them
  LAB-004 Identifiers make the intent addressable
  LAB-016 Resolution check before freezing
  LAB-023 No silent loss
Stamped by `labkit-init exp <name>` (no --model); fill the TODOs, keep the structure.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import hashlib
import json
